Cloud Monitoring and Alerts in Cloud Computing

Cloud monitoring and alerts are essential components of cloud infrastructure management, helping organizations track performance, security, and resource usage in real time. These tools enable proactive issue resolution by notifying administrators of potential problems before they impact users.


---

1. What is Cloud Monitoring?

Cloud monitoring involves tracking and analyzing the performance, availability, and security of cloud-based services, applications, and infrastructure. It helps ensure that cloud resources operate efficiently and meet service level agreements (SLAs).

Key Aspects of Cloud Monitoring

✅ Performance Monitoring – Tracks CPU usage, memory, network latency, and response times.
✅ Security Monitoring – Detects unauthorized access, DDoS attacks, and unusual traffic.
✅ Application Monitoring – Observes application response times, errors, and dependencies.
✅ Infrastructure Monitoring – Checks the health of virtual machines (VMs), databases, and storage systems.
✅ Cost Monitoring – Helps optimize cloud spending by tracking resource usage.

Cloud Monitoring Tools

AWS CloudWatch (for AWS services)

Google Cloud Operations Suite (formerly Stackdriver)

Azure Monitor (for Azure cloud services)

